{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1478030-aeon-homebrew-help-playable-hiveminds","id":1478030,"title":"[Aeon] Homebrew Help: Playable Hiveminds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-04T21:29:42-07:00","id":1478030,"title":"[Aeon] Homebrew Help: Playable Hiveminds","content":"I'll cut to the chase:<br /> <br /> How would one write balanced rules for a species that is effectively composed of hiveminds - as in, each individual ego is one hive of genetically identical bodies and their queen? Seems a bit hard to balance literally playing a bunch of people with the same personality who operate with perfect coordination.<br /> <br /> I'm inspired by the sandkings from the George RR Martin story of the same name, which also has an interesting take on how religion works and would result in a unique spiritual perspective - they effectively start off as semi-sentient ants who can psionically sense more intelligent beings, and if that being gives them food, they tend to conclude that being is a god, even building altars in their nests. Once they mold into sapient adults, they catch on to the error, but they remember their past as ants. It's a semi-horror story, so what happens is that our rich asshole protagonist buys some larval sandking nests as exotic pets and turns their terrarium into what is effectively a dogfighting ring, and making the survivors feral berserkers - the ending is when an adult molt who escaped before things got really bad spots him when escaping the most rabid nest, and promptly repays all the misery they suffered at their &quot;god&quot;. Obviously, in Aeon, things might turn out better (and even in-universe, it generally does - there's a normal, friendly adult sandking hive involved, and their partner describes the rabid hive as likely criminally insane by the species' standard), but that is a wonderful starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T23:58:16-07:00","id":1478035,"title":"","content":"I would suggest you to use a \u201cscale of numbers\u201d approach, with the big number of members, when dealing together with an challenge where their numbers are relevant, add scale to the action.<br /> <br /> If you had a big number of different members, than using the telepathy power to share knowledge and skills would fit better, but, as they are all virtually drones of a all powerful queen, they can be all set as a single character with scale due to numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"us